From: Cryolitia PukNgae <cryolitia.pukngae@linux.dev>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 07:41:25 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: qrtr: Unwind MHI receive buffer setup on resume failure

When an initial IPCR receive buffer fails to queue, MHI has not taken
ownership of it. Release that buffer immediately. On resume, undo
mhi_prepare_for_transfer() if receive buffer setup fails, matching the
probe path. Unpreparing returns any buffers already queued through the
existing channel reset callback.

This prevents partially started channels from surviving failed resume
and allows a later transfer preparation to start with empty rings.

Codex found and implemented the unwind and validated allocation and
queue failures at each position of a four-buffer ring using
source-based ASan/UBSan tests and the ARM64 QRTR MHI module build.

Fixes: 51731792a25c ("net: qrtr: Drop the MHI auto_queue feature for IPCR DL channels")
Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Cryolitia PukNgae <cryolitia.pukngae@linux.dev>
---
 net/qrtr/mhi.c | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/net/qrtr/mhi.c b/net/qrtr/mhi.c
index e9a4bb9..c55705d 100644
--- a/net/qrtr/mhi.c
+++ b/net/qrtr/mhi.c
@@ -99,6 +99,7 @@ static int qcom_mhi_qrtr_queue_dl_buffers(struct mhi_device *mhi_dev)
 				    MHI_EOT);
 		if (ret) {
 			dev_err(&mhi_dev->dev, "Failed to queue buffer: %d\n", ret);
+			devm_kfree(&mhi_dev->dev, buf);
 			return ret;
 		}
 	}
@@ -203,8 +204,10 @@ static int __maybe_unused qcom_mhi_qrtr_pm_resume_early(struct device *dev)
 	}
 
 	rc = qcom_mhi_qrtr_queue_dl_buffers(mhi_dev);
-	if (rc)
+	if (rc) {
+		mhi_unprepare_from_transfer(mhi_dev);
 		return rc;
+	}
 
 	qrtr_endpoint_hello(&qdev->ep);
 
